# Badge Deactivation Closeout Rule

## Current Model

Week-8 Q2 closeout preview frames **badge deactivation** for **Pier 9 contractors** as a mandatory step before Juno Castillo signs off the **Q2 Terminal Readiness Playbook**. Temporary contractor badges issued during P9-GATE commissioning — including Fatima Okonkwo's 14-badge Turnstile batch from May 11 — must be revoked at closeout alongside any remaining Bridgeway gangway crew access. Juno owns finalizing the closeout section by Wednesday of week 8; Glenn Wexler and Victor Dunn review open punch lists in parallel but badge revocation routes through Fatima's access system.

## Evidence

- `2026-06-08-q2-closeout-preview` - Week 8 preview before playbook sign-off and **Pier 9 contractor badge deactivation**; Juno action to finalize Q2 playbook closeout section by Wed; open punch list covers P9-GATE gate delivery landed May 28 with Cal's floodlight commissioning window and P9-GANG load cert still with Priya; Marcus wants Friday Harbor berth restored once ramp handover signs.

## Use In Work

- Include Pier 9 contractor **badge deactivation** in every Q2 closeout checklist — coordinate with Fatima Okonkwo to revoke temp badges before archiving the terminal readiness playbook.
- Cross-reference the May 11 P9-GATE badge batch against the deactivation list so no Turnstile or Bridgeway contractor retains staging access after commissioning completes.

## Limits

This closeout rule covers Pier 9 contractor temp badges only — not HarborPass migration access windows, Pier 7 legacy barcode reader sunset on 2026-06-12, or ongoing night-harbormaster staging logs Cal Donner maintains.

## Connections

- [[plan-q2-terminal-readiness]] - Standing plan whose week-8 checkpoint includes Pier 9 badge deactivation before archive.
