# Juno Castillo ↔ Elena Vasquez

## Current Model

Juno Castillo reports informally to Elena Vasquez on fleet-impacting terminal work — drydock windows, sea-trial milestones, and berth holds that affect MV Seaglass sailings. When Elena Vasquez opened the **SG-REFIT drydock** on **2026-05-18**, Juno was on the distribution and coordinated berth 4 heavy-lift zone exclusivity through refit sea trial. Juno does not own drydock approvals but implements Elena's fleet constraints in the Q2 Terminal Readiness Playbook berth schedule. Fuel-system purge sequencing and crane booking corrections surface in separate syncs after drydock opens.

## Evidence

- `2026-05-18-drydock-window-opens` - Elena Vasquez email opens **SG-REFIT drydock** officially as of that morning with **drydock window 2026-05-18** starting now; berth 4 heavy-lift zone is Seaglass-only through refit sea trial; Victor Hale confirms spare thrust bearing crate port-side with hull penetration deferred to morning sync; Juno on distribution for fleet-impacting berth coordination.

## Use In Work

- Escalate berth 4 holds, SG-REFIT milestone timing, and any terminal schedule change that blocks MV Seaglass to Elena Vasquez rather than resolving at pier-lead level.
- Cross-check Juno's playbook berth grid against Elena's approved drydock window before booking competing heavy-lift work at berth 4.

## Limits

This escalation path covers fleet and drydock work only — Pier 7 passenger ramp messaging routes to Elena Crane, and Pier 9 infrastructure staging aligns with Victor Dunn. Juno does not co-sign SG-REFIT engineering milestones; Elena Vasquez and Victor Hale do.

## Connections

- [[juno-castillo]] - Senior Terminal Operations Manager who escalates fleet-impacting work upward.
- [[elena-vasquez]] - Fleet Maintenance Director who approves drydock windows and co-signs refit milestones.
- [[sg-refit]] - MV Seaglass engine-room refit whose drydock window defines this escalation boundary.
- [[decision-drydock-window]] - Formal approval opening SG-REFIT drydock on 2026-05-18 that Juno implements.
